      "writtenOn": "2024-11-14T00:28:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A lot of method are updated to now require the BLUETOOTH_PRIVILEGED as conditional.\n\nI believe we should not do that. There may be one or two that actually can enforce BLUETOOTH_PRIVILEGED because of the offload requirement, but most of the already existing API will never enforce it.\n\nOne exemple of solving that is `BluetoothAdapter.disable()` that doesn\u0027t require PRIVILEGED despite calling a method that can depending on the parameter.\n\nhttps://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Bluetooth/framework/java/android/bluetooth/BluetoothAdapter.java;l\u003d1726;drc\u003d891fea7286c9e0ebe376e1554afcb288eed366eb\n\nThis may not be the best solution here, since the annotation was added in a lot of location, we may want to narrow down only to the method that could enforce the permission, and if it is too wide, try to update internal implementation to have something more focused",
      "revId": "e948788db2d31ab8917baa577b47f2e335aff61b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
