      "writtenOn": "2024-11-14T01:27:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In build time, BLUETOOTH_PRIVILEGED was required for the APIs which can call BluetoothSocketManagerBinder::connectSocket() or BluetoothSocketManagerBinder::createSocketChannel() where I added the enforcement of BLUETOOTH_PRIVILEGED.\n\n```\nif (dataPath !\u003d BluetoothSocketSettings.DATA_PATH_NO_OFFLOAD) {\n    mService.enforceCallingOrSelfPermission(BLUETOOTH_PRIVILEGED, null);\n}\n```\n\nTo reduce updating many methods, I can create separate methods in BluetoothSocketManagerBinder that requires BLUETOOTH_PRIVILEGED. Then, only few methods using offload socket option can reach out to the new methods with the annotation of BLUETOOTH_PRIVILEGED. Does it make sense?\n\n```\nBluetoothSocketManagerBinder::connectSocketExt() \nBluetoothSocketManagerBinder::createSocketChannelExt()\n```",
      "parentUuid": "fb03578f_d0e7d348",
      "revId": "e948788db2d31ab8917baa577b47f2e335aff61b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
